.TH idt 1M "December 2025" "IRIX NVMe Driver 0.9.4"
.SH NAME
idt \- Disk performance tester for IRIX NVMe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBidt\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I idt
is an interactive disk performance testing utility for IRIX 6.5 that
benchmarks disk I/O performance using different workload modes and
access patterns. It uses pthreads for multi-threaded testing and
provides real-time performance statistics.
.PP
The utility supports three distinct workload modes:
.IP \(bu 2
One file per thread - each thread operates on its own file
.IP \(bu 2
Shared file with per-thread regions - all threads share a single file
with divided regions
.IP \(bu 2
Raw device per thread - each thread accesses a raw device or partition
.PP
.I idt
runs interactively, prompting the user for all configuration options
including workload type, file paths, number of threads, test duration,
block size, I/O mode (read/write), and access pattern (sequential/random).
.PP
Performance results are logged to timestamped files in the diskperf_logs
directory and displayed on screen during and after test execution.
.SH OPTIONS
.I idt
currently operates in fully interactive mode with no command-line
options. All configuration is done through interactive prompts.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
During test execution, the following keyboard commands are available:
.TP
.B l
Display one-shot per-thread performance snapshot (prints once and logs)
.TP
.B L
Toggle continuous per-second per-thread live statistics on/off
.TP
.B q
Request early test termination
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the disk performance tester interactively:
.PP
.nf
idt
.PP
The program will prompt for:
.IP \(bu 2
Workload option (1=one file per thread, 2=shared file, 3=raw device)
.IP \(bu 2
File or device path (may use %d placeholder for thread number)
.IP \(bu 2
Number of threads (1-128)
.IP \(bu 2
Test duration in seconds
.IP \(bu 2
Block size in bytes (512 to 16MB)
.IP \(bu 2
I/O mode (read or write)
.IP \(bu 2
Access pattern (sequential or random)
.IP \(bu 2
Pre-allocation size in MB (workload-dependent)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I diskperf_logs/run_YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS.log
Timestamped log files containing detailed test results
